# Line endings, made deterministic for every clone regardless of the
# cloner's core.autocrlf, in Frazaro's shape. The repository stores LF; the
# working copy gets what each consumer needs:
#   - Rust, its manifests, the toolchain file and the host shim are LF on
#     every platform, as rustfmt writes them.
#   - A cartridge is VLA (.vla) and gets CRLF on checkout, as Frazaro's
#     corpus files do, so that the language's reference implementation,
#     whose line reader treats a bare LF as text, can read a cartridge too.
#   - A built .wasm is bytes.
# Everything else is ordinary text (LF in the repo, the platform's default
# on checkout) or binary.
* text=auto
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.vla text eol=crlf
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
